  mistake the reader will just look at the  cutoff and if the reader value is higher  than the cutoff that that's really  called positive so using a reader is  very useful again to prevent subjective  analysis and interpretation of the  results this test will be very suitable  for programs to prevent mother-to-child  transmission and to support the fight  against the rising syphilis infection in  high-risk patients as you can see this  is very important to note that the  performance of this duplex test is as  good as the performance of separate HIV  and syphilis test 99.9% sensitivity and  100% on various whole blood and plasma  and for HIV syphilis 100% finger stick  blood and 99% and 100% of serum venous  or blood and plasma the test has been  used outside of the US for several years  and many studies have been performed and  in the two slides that I'm going to show  you now we are going to look at the  results of meta-analysis of laboratory  and field studies of this test in  various countries a studies were  performed shown by the CDC song by the  University of California Los Angeles in  Brazil makes  sico peru jana and malawi seven of those  studies didn't use the reader at the  time the results were interpreted  visually after we introduced the reader  the age study was performed and used  both the visual interpretation and  reader based interpretation below me for  a comparison of the two interpretation  methods you can see the tables on this  slide that show the results obtained for  each of the eight studies and under the  tables the aggregated sensitivity and  specificity of the studies for HIV  ninety-nine point fourteen percent  sensitivity and ninety-eight point 82  percent specificity and for syphilis  ninety six twenty four percent  sensitivity in ninety nine point five  nine percent specificity so those  results again in an aggregated form  confirm all the results that have been  shown in the previous slides of this  presentation of the two tables at the  bottom we can see the results obtained  with the reader and again for HIV they  are very well in line with the  aggregated results that I just presented  for syphilis  it looks like the sensitivity is a  little lower but we're talking about one  false positive sample on 142 samples  total and that may be due to various  reasons maybe one being that it was the  first time that we were using the reader  in the field and when we look at the  specificity it is as good as the one  obtained with visual results so overall  we can say that the result obtained by  the reader are similar to those obtained  visually  in conclusion a combination repeat test  for the detection of antibodies to HIV  and to syphilis at the point-of-care  works very well and as well as separate  tests and it delivers the same levels of  sensitivity and specificity the two dose  of separate repeat tests now let's look  for a few moments and highly multiplexed  rapid tests here for the detection of  pathogens that provoke similar symptoms  of fever in due to several diseases and  in this case it's the DPP fever I know  for Africa the seven pathogens include  Ebola Lhasa and Marburg which are three  deadly diseases chikungunya dengue and  Zika which are also endemic to Africa  and malaria which is also found in the  same areas where Ebola Lhasa and Marburg  are found it's very important to put all  those seven pathogens on the same test  because at the beginning at the onset of  the disease those seven pathogens  present with the same symptoms in  patients and so it's very difficult to  diagnose those diseases based on  symptoms only and as you can understand  it's very important when you triage  patients in a zone where Ebola is  present for instance that you can  discriminate very rapidly and  efficiently between Ebola and let's say  malaria so that we say the patient's can  be separated and treated differently the  results will be interpreted with the DPP  micro reader to provide an objective  read of the result and avoid any  misinterpretation by the users and also  because when you have a cartridge with a  number of the slides on the same string  you want to be sure that there is no  transcription error by reading multiple  tests from multiple lines that are  close to each other in this slide we  show the results from a study that was  aimed at analyzing the performance of  the malaria component of the multiplex  test we have made several studies and  during each of the study we analyzed  separates analytes like Ebola  for instance in malaria so in this case  we see the results from a malaria study  which took place both in Africa and in  Peru in South America and you can see on  the table on the right that the two  components for malaria the HRP protein  and the pea LDH analyte give as good if  not better performance as those obtained  with w-h-o pre-qualified malaria rapid  diagnostic tests 98.6% of the samples  were detected by H R P 2 and 4 p LD h  which we know is a lower performing  analyte we were very close to 80%  performance we are working hard on  creating more applications of the DPP  technology so that are those assays can  be used in the field and can be used on  millions of people who need them in the  areas where malaria dengue chikungunya  are endemic and you can see here several  examples of the the expanded format with  the two test test strips or the single  format on the bottom line you can see  examples of DBP zika tests looking for  IgM presence on the top window and IgG  presence in the bottom window same for  dengue or chikungunya and on the right  you can see a cassette that includes the  tree DPB zika chikungunya and dengue IgM  and I di Gigi detection test on the  bottom you can see antigen test so in  this case we're not looking at the IgM  presence or AGG but the antigens to zika  dengue and chikungunya on a single  cartridge or dengue and a swamp antigen  or again IgM only for zika dengue and  chikungunya or Zika by itself each of  those combinations has it's particularly  important feel field of interest by the  various countries and various regions  they can be used in areas where some  disease is endemic or where there is an  outbreak or they can be used like the  DPP's de Cadenet chikungunya combination  test for APD epidemiological studies so  in conclusion I think that Kristin and I  have presented to you the next  generation of lateral flow test the  generation that allows for high  performance high sensitivity  quantitation connectivity and  multiplexing and by combining together  the power of the DPP lateral flow  technology with multiplexing and with  the benefit of a reader we are we are  able to offer who are customers and to  millions of patients the DPP system I  want to thank you for being with us  today and if you have any questions we  will feel free to send them to us and we  will reply to you via email thank you  very much
 

